===={{MangaArc|Red, Green & Blue}}====
A child resembling a Bug Catcher appeared in [[Pallet Town]] in ''[[PS001|A Glimpse of the Glow]]''.

In ''[[PS012|Wake Up—You're Snorlax!]]'', a Bug Catcher appeared during the [[Miracle Cycle]] [[bicycle]] race, alongside a {{tc|Swimmer}} and {{adv|Red}}. He took a shortcut through a small woods full of Bug Pokémon, but later got stuck on {{rt|12|Kanto}} due to a sleeping [[Snor]]lax blocking the way.

===={{MangaArc|Emerald}}====
In ''[[PS319|Verily Vanquishing Vileplume I]]'', a Bug Catcher named James (Mikiya in the [[Chuang Yi]] translation) was seen battling {{tc|Battle Girl}} Cyndy in the [[Battle Dome]]. While it is unknown who won, what is known is that James at some point lost a match, eliminating him from the tournament.

===={{MangaArc|HeartGold & SoulSilver}}====
In ''[[PS442|Out-Odding Oddish]]'', a Bug Catcher was seen listening to [[DJ Mary]]'s announcement at the [[Pokéathlon Dome]]. In the same chapter, another Bug Catcher with a {{p|Beedrill}} was seen entering the Pokéathlon Dome.

In ''[[PS446|Weavile Wobbles But It Won't Fall Down]]'', a Bug Catcher was seen exploring the [[Safari Zone Gate]].

===={{MangaArc|Diamond & Pearl}}====
In ''[[PS390|Licking Lickitung]]'', a Bug Catcher appeared during the [[Pokétch]] presentation taking place in [[Jubilife City]].

===={{MangaArc|Platinum}}====
A Bug Catcher appeared in ''[[PS418|Deprogramming Porygon-Z]]'', where he was part of a group of people who entered the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|IV}} after [[Palmer]] had his assistants open the gates.

